  "launches": [
    {
      "id": 79274,
      "title": "Greptile: AI expert that understands large codebases",
      "tagline": "Platform that lets engineers understand large codebases and build internal dev tools using AI.",
      "body": "Hi everyone! We’re [Soohoon](https://linkedin.com/in/soohoonchoi), [Vaishant](https://linkedin.com/in/vaishant), and [Daksh](https://linkedin.com/in/dakshg) from [Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/). We are building the AI expert on any codebase.\n\n**tl;dr** Greptile is an AI platform that lets LLMs understand large codebases. Teams and devs at 250+ companies including Stripe and Amazon use it to get answers to questions about large codebases via our web app, automatically update their docs, build PR review bots on our API, and more. **Try it now → [**app.greptile.com**](https://app.greptile.com)**\n\n![](https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/fuO2un8RYVAWc1rG4KjNOKUfudaWA7z4ZKG7kDK7-PcX8zzPOUunZHPD4vLCSfEOYp0WQ00vfigNq3ivhFBPbgFsbH-ldXa8VQLVr0FcA3r3kQDgPMCtfrVzpjSZ5RWYaagrIQYahicZPMx-Fgc1HQM)\n\n### **PROBLEM**\n\nAs software companies grow:\n\n1. Codebases get more **complex**.\n2. **Legacy code** and **tech debt** accumulates.\n3. Docs are usually **outdated**.\n4. **Original engineers leave**, and new engineers are less familiar with the code.\n\nTo get around this, developers:\n\n1. Just brute force their way to grokking the code - which is hard and time-consuming.\n2. Seek help from the subject matter expert, which is difficult if they have left, work remotely, or are just busy.\n3. Try to use tools like GitHub copilot, which are not designed to answer with full code context, so they fail to deliver.\n\nIn fact, the thing that makes coding hard is usually the codebase, not the code!\n\nWe found a way to index and search large codebases such that LLMs can always find the right context, allowing any developer to build internal developer tools powered by AI.\n\nHere’s Felix from Twenty (open source CRM with 9k GitHub stars).\n\n![](https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/_rr-le-rqZZzZQoT6p1gikSOdZjaAAKzSwfmn4j9qs7VuKb9Gcw9jnTNfcofYa9F0OaFpSPl3JAmA_hZE6dnV-aBgGTgspfrqILEcAsHrqqMr7g8JuB_YeCMWmCikptC3eWHPgXFzEAPR1gWT_GAtEE)\n\n### **🦎 Greptile in action →**\n\nHere are some ways engineers use Greptile 👇\n\n1. **Narek from** **Lantern** **(W24):** grokking PostgreSQL’s source code, which Lantern is built on.\n2. **Rahul from** **AgentHub (W24):** parsing OSS frameworks that AgentHub integrates with.\n3. **Jack Chapman from** **Cardinal Gray** **(S23):** generating E2E test cases for multi-file services.\n4. **Isaiah Granet from Bland AI (S23):** integrating with the Twilio node SDK.\n5. **SWE at Thera (S22):** writing new features that require complex, multi-file changes.\n6. **YC Medtech (S15):** building an internal PR review bot on top of our API.\n7. **SWE at Stripe (S09):** debugging internal Rust libraries.\n8. **Principal Engineer at Microsoft:** reviewing his team’s code (open source).\n9. **TMO (old B2B software company):** working with their legacy .NET code.\n\n### **ASK →**\n\n* If you’re a developer working with large codebases - try Greptile here → [app.greptile.com](http://app.greptile.com)\n* If you want Greptile at your org, email me ([daksh@greptile.com](mailto:daksh@greptile.com)) or book a demo on my calendar ([greptile.com/demo](http://greptile.com/demo))\n\n![](https://lh7-us.googleusercontent.com/zintlEJgFJVQK3d_FV8Qi3zb845wA5TgCwqcv3jrXyH9N1YNFBFLOlBRPT76Mf16_hilA6DC5wmu9BcNqWPfilKj_52ex2WFjWoHUf6vkZKFll86vU4D1vVYgEOUGWTw-qMqkmeCyMpyAvpUQLiWL6I)\n\n",
      "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/launches/Kcc-greptile-ai-expert-that-understands-large-codebases",
      "votes": 48,
      "created_at": "2024-03-11T20:06:39.485Z"
